-- CK-216: `markup_type_in_foreign` (checker-v2.md §25.2) finds the markup
-- type wherever a `foreign`'s declared type holds it, after aliases: in a
-- record's field (`platform/Render.beni` 21:13), through a record alias
-- (23:13), in a custom type's constructor (25:13), through a recursive
-- custom type whose constructors reach it only through another (27:13),
-- and beside a type whose expansion is thousands of positions wide
-- (33:13). `plain` and `recursive`, which hold no markup, are accepted. On
-- the base the search looked through applications, tuples and functions
-- only, and gave up after 4 096 positions answering "no markup", so all
-- five were accepted.
import Node exposing (Program)


main : Program
main =
    Node.print "hello"
